      "sha1": "",
      "snippet": "\nJustice Stevens\ndelivered the opinion of the Court.\nThe Sixth and Fourteenth Amendments of our Constitution guarantee that a person brought to trial in any state or federal court must be afforded the right to the assistance of counsel before he can be validly convicted and punished by imprisonment.1 In Faretta v. California, 422 U. S. 806 (1975), we decided that the defe",
