      "ordering_key": 2,
      "per_curiam": false,
      "sha1": "",
      "snippet": "\nJustice Kennedy,\nconcurring.\nTo resolve this case it is unnecessary to cast doubt upon the rationale of Faretta v. California, 422 U. S. 806 (1975). Faretta can be accepted as quite sound, yet it does not follow that a convicted person has a similar right of self-representation on appeal. Different considerations apply in the appellate system, and the Court explains why this is so.",
